# Purpose
Keep React components consistent, maintainable, and optimized for web (desktop + mobile browsers).

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO use functional components with hooks; avoid class components.
DO design for mobile-first: base styles for small screens, then add min-width breakpoints for larger.
DO ensure touch targets are at least 44×44px for interactive elements (buttons, links, inputs).
DO use semantic HTML (main, nav, header, section, article, button, a) for accessibility.
DO extract reusable logic into custom hooks; keep components focused on rendering.
DO use React.memo or useMemo/useCallback only when profiling shows a benefit; avoid premature optimization.

### DON'T
MUST NOT rely on fixed pixel widths for layouts; use relative units (rem, %, min/max) and flex/grid.
MUST NOT assume desktop viewport; test at 320px, 375px, 768px, 1024px+.
MUST NOT inline large objects/arrays in JSX (creates new refs on each render); extract to constants or memoize.

## Breakpoints (recommended)
```css
/* Mobile-first */
@media (min-width: 640px) { /* sm */ }
@media (min-width: 768px) { /* md */ }
@media (min-width: 1024px) { /* lg */ }
@media (min-width: 1280px) { /* xl */ }
```

## Completion Checklist
[ ] Components are functional and use hooks.
[ ] Layouts are responsive (no hardcoded widths that break on mobile).
[ ] Touch targets meet 44×44px minimum.
[ ] Semantic HTML used where applicable.
